course: dictionary
lesson: 3376
title: Exhaustion: tired right out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exhaustion means being extremely tired, with no energy left. It can also mean that something has been completely used up. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits. «Olivia felt exhaustion after the race» tells you she was worn out.
explain: The clue words are often next to it. «Heat exhaustion» is a health problem from getting too hot and losing too much water. «Burnout is exhaustion from too much stress for too long.» The words from too much stress tell you the cause, so ask yourself what is causing it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Heat exhaustion is more than just being sleepy: it can make you dizzy, sick and sweaty. Context shows you how serious the word is.
fact: Exhaustion means being extremely tired, with no energy left.
fact: Exhaustion can also mean something is completely used up, like «the exhaustion of the oil supply».
fact: «Heat exhaustion» means feeling weak, dizzy and sick from too much heat.
fact: «Burnout» means exhaustion from too much stress for too long, usually from work.
fact: Exhaustion is a noun you cannot count: you say «great exhaustion», not «three exhaustions».
exercise: What does exhaustion mean? | A kind of sweet food | *Being extremely tired, with no energy left | Being very loud and noisy
exercise: «Burnout is exhaustion from too much stress for too long.» What usually causes burnout? | A hot, sunny day at the beach | Eating too many sweets | *Too much stress for too long, often from work
exercise: Olivia feels dizzy, sick and sweaty after running in the heat. What is the best first step? | Eat a big meal | Run another race to warm up | Ignore it until it goes away by itself | *Find some shade, lie down and sip some water
test: In «collapse with exhaustion», what does exhaustion mean? | Hiding away from everyone | A type of heavy coat | *Being completely worn out | Being very happy and excited
test: «The exhaustion of the oil supply» means what? | Oil is being given away free | *Oil is being completely used up | Oil is becoming cheaper
exam: Which phrase names an illness caused by getting too hot? | Exhaustion of the oil supply | *Heat exhaustion | Burnout from work
